      "id": "STB-01",
      "chapter": "inputs",
      "title": "Eliminating all weights above one",
      "anchor": "inputs-stable-rank",
      "statement": "At odd homological degree m=2e+1, zSeq after m−1 steps multiplies a stable weight-j functional by the product of (ℓ^j−ℓ^i), 2≤i≤m. Thus all weights 2,…,m vanish. In odd degree the invariant-form decomposition has at most one weight-one cyclic-trace functional per infinite place.",
      "hypotheses": "For the recurrence ℓ is a positive integer, and in the application ℓ is prime. The weight system vanishes on boundaries, is unchanged by standard block inclusions and scales by d^j under d repeated blocks. The invariant-form statement applies in odd degree over a number field.",
