    {
      "id": "STB-02",
      "chapter": "inputs",
      "title": "How the r₂ coordinate bound reaches the Bockstein fiber",
      "anchor": "inputs-stable-place-tests",
      "statement": "Over the ring of integers of a totally complex L′, with m odd, m<r₂ and n≥2m+4, the integral rank of the span of zSeq outputs in H_m(GL_{ℓ^(m−1)n}) is at most r₂. For m=3, n=10, ℓ=2, L′=ℚ(ζ₂₀), the free contribution to a q-torsion evaluation target has cardinality at most q^4.",
      "hypotheses": "Ordinary degree-m homological stability over the Dedekind ring of integers. In addition to stable injectivity the proof uses separation by real cocycles and representation of their cycle evaluations by invariant forms after further stabilization. Integral rank counts torsion-free directions. The separate torsion factors and field enlargement retain their hypotheses in the degree-two application.",
